# POC-VMS-41 preexecution freeze audit

- Confirm the command starts no Devin session and makes no model, DB, Redis, Seven, Target Solver, network-by-candidate, or subagent call.
- Confirm the full solve-side unittest suite passes with zero skips and the 161-file protected intake baseline is rehashed before any freeze artifact is committed.
- Confirm the resolved Devin binary/version/catalog, exact `glm-5-2` / High encoding and the user-level Devin AGENTS path/size/hash are frozen.
- Confirm all four case/source/acceptable-set bindings, code/assets/tests/protocol hashes, four unique attempt IDs, resource contract, side-effect limits and one D-volume result root are present.
- Confirm the protocol is finalized first and the separate manifest binds its hash; the protocol never embeds its own hash.
- Confirm the three live-fixture outputs are append-once/idempotent for identical bytes, and drift or an existing live/partial result fails closed.
